#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161745 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "6d3ad56f-a242-5335-aa48-e2608b1b973d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16584" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(1\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/f3/f3440005b2b4e7ce1cc2eed5825d11cb309522a6807bcd18ffada189fadd0cda.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( 1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/1f/1f2f28b0f36aeb85a07076e1507c9561b707bf7d00de727998b02075b5458da4.svg)\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-x}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.8647\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161746 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "f1adfc5c-78aa-5f14-bec5-cf763d86e5af" :question/math-academy-id "e-16585" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(\\dfrac 23\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/49/49fa146efc8029727469bc5909c2a946c9cb96383976d4096d455b423a428479.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( \\dfrac 23 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/72/721ca1810b816431f99bb8294f4ad12ff125342640a925035487c8ecace4eff6.svg)Therefore, we can calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-2x/3}|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161747 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c89beba-5605-514e-82c3-8e8145b178c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval Using the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "fffe6dba-c0a1-5644-a975-6d51b6de2f98" :question/math-academy-id "e-16586" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(2\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/e7/e77daa45c1026175eec99e71cb336ad5b8c2a46683170b0f9357a4ad7e9d1bf5.svg)\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left( 2 \\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/e0/e0b6d1388350fabce97f26601d512e60cfe6ac3ab41230671718ca034c5c3860.svg)Therefore, we can calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}<X<2) & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{{e}^{-2x}|}_{1/2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4}+{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.3496\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161748 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/id #uuid "88232e58-999e-5ac8-8f09-8a4b204ec51c" :question/math-academy-id "e-16587" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(4\\right),$ calculate $P\\left(X \\leq 7 \\, \\bigg |\\, X > 5\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(\\lambda)$ and two positive real numbers $s, t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\, \\big |\\, X>s) = P(X > t) = e^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\leq s+t \\, \\big|\\, X>s) = 1-P(X>s+t \\, \\big |\\, X>s) = 1-e^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda = 4,$ $s=5,$ and $s+t=7.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt = (t+s) - s =7 - 5 = 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7\\,|\\,X>5) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(4)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-8} \\\\  & ≈0.999\\,664.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31d5edd8-2b29-5eba-8a70-917a5b0f20f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423969} {:answer/id #uuid "71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423978} {:answer/id #uuid "a4655f58-d989-5a50-8b84-0a0259d6d8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{e}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423984} {:answer/id #uuid "a59b312d-c446-5a83-97bf-18385fce9ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{9}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423985} {:answer/id #uuid "bd231bf4-aff5-5dd1-9238-2dee00cd6f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423978} :answer-field/id #uuid "37078ec0-a9a2-5952-8060-4f2067bef6bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "840fc6bd-43f7-5e1f-9678-e0daa00596e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-253929" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X>6\\,|\\,X>4).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the momeryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=6.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=6-4=2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6\\,|\\,X>4) & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(2)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00532a77-8369-5069-a645-da39692238cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423964} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba4d575-3c96-585c-87ae-967c1404dc69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423975} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf46d04-45a1-535e-a92e-c9cb35404ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423976} {:answer/id #uuid "950530ce-1ae8-509e-b4cd-ed8ae399b36c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423981} {:answer/id #uuid "e23b4a6b-fba0-5d93-9ac6-0cd62b1a9f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e23b4a6b-fba0-5d93-9ac6-0cd62b1a9f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423990} :answer-field/id #uuid "e05b810e-c24f-55a7-bef2-0f820b29550d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6017236-d9af-57fe-9a24-c8e569cb2642" :question/math-academy-id "q-253938" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>6).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=6,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-6=3\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>6) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(2)\\cdot (3)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b36bf296-2266-53e1-ae35-e8fa637db296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2650" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161403} {:answer/id #uuid "d4524de5-3262-560c-b7b4-1f0fe461930f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2889" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161404} {:answer/id #uuid "eedb40f3-78bd-5fd3-9379-cf524faf4299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161405} {:answer/id #uuid "0022f9f8-4785-58b8-a095-8f6a00b57ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2835" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161406} {:answer/id #uuid "28030f6a-21a7-5d71-8fac-6aff6f4139ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0022f9f8-4785-58b8-a095-8f6a00b57ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2835" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161406} :answer-field/id #uuid "87973830-c545-5416-8045-ac11b74dd853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45110329-7387-51ad-ab6c-5c96036db67b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96344" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{6}).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<\\frac{1}{6})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{1}{6}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/6}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}{|}_{0}^{1/6} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1/3}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.2835\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a753c6c-3899-5081-81c1-9c51956a63b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423967} {:answer/id #uuid "39d93c58-7d48-5de8-9930-8560bb4ab222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5932" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423970} {:answer/id #uuid "b5df255f-d5f8-5d26-a865-2d00936b6ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6585" :db/id #edb/ref 175