e $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{2}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1<X<4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<4) & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1745b6-630b-529f-9136-c40f62c94d25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2231" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423968} {:answer/id #uuid "3f517b2d-d281-5139-846d-3d24808ad7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0821" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423972} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7853be-90ec-5040-a947-22a3b32a3ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6065" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423980} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423988} {:answer/id #uuid "e72eff5e-65c2-554e-894e-cea3af368c6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8647" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd0cfc25-ccc8-5d6f-a075-ad935990a0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423988} :answer-field/id #uuid "06adbee9-5f6f-500e-9c80-babe38453b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0be3a602-67d5-5cf7-8f80-aff71640198e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96406" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(X\\ge 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\ge 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b8a2e77-056b-5c7d-a4a5-f0b85875f98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0498" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423971} {:answer/id #uuid "4e91c1c2-03b1-5f7b-accf-22d6915d4b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2865" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423974} {:answer/id #uuid "95ffeb01-adda-57d6-881e-fcb39a8b7a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0067" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423982} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423983} {:answer/id #uuid "f083723d-90d7-5c3f-8b0b-f6cf96ee2b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3679" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423983} :answer-field/id #uuid "0782fde0-7971-5f6d-aba6-4b1f607a9ca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e3c60ce-47c9-5c4f-b8dd-973c8222fab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96407" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $U∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(U\\ge 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $U$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nU∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(U\\ge 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2u}{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-6} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c89beba-5605-514e-82c3-8e8145b178c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval Using the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a50814-795d-5d28-8e92-209754c2af10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3654" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423965} {:answer/id #uuid "20637901-6ccf-5b0b-8845-93cfcc926093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3611" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423966} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1edc2d-b633-52ba-85a7-13aec31489a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1286" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423973} {:answer/id #uuid "6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1329" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423977} {:answer/id #uuid "78e06ba4-70f9-51bf-9980-6444eb5316e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1358" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1329" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423977} :answer-field/id #uuid "64885566-dbce-53b8-b813-e5b5f9f5627a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "548f5527-3c2c-5249-846d-012dddb74912" :question/math-academy-id "q-96417" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6}+{e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1329\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
